    <name>
      <text>Matrix geometric series and TB transmission - matrix inputs</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Matrix geometric series and TB transmission</h3>

<p>
Tuberculosis transmission between Nairobi and Mombasa is modelled by the matrix
\\(
A={@A@}.
\\)
If
\\(
x_n={@x_symbol@}
\\)
represents the active TB cases in generation \(n\), where the first row is Nairobi and the second row is Mombasa, then
\\(
x_{n+1}=Ax_n.
\\)
</p>

<p>The initial outbreak is
\[
x_0={@x0@}.
\]</p>

<p><b>1.</b> Compute the next generation \(x_1=Ax_0\).</p>
<p>Enter your answer as a column matrix, for example <code>matrix([1],[2])</code>.</p>
<p>
[[input:ansX1]]
[[validation:ansX1]]
[[feedback:prtX1]]
</p>

<p><b>2.</b> Compute the following generation \(x_2=Ax_1=A^2x_0\).</p>
<p>
[[input:ansX2]]
[[validation:ansX2]]
[[feedback:prtX2]]
</p>

<p><b>3.</b> Rearrange the lines to prove the matrix geometric series formula.</p>
<p>
We are proving that, if \(A^{n+1}\to 0\), then
\[
I+A+A^2+\cdots=(I-A)^{-1}.
\]
</p>

[[parsons input="ansProof" height="420px" width="100%"]]
{# parsons_encode(proof_steps) #}
[[/parsons]]

<p style="display:none;">
[[input:ansProof]] [[validation:ansProof]] [[feedback:prtProof]]
</p>

<p><b>4.</b> Compute \(I-A\).</p>
<p>Enter your answer as a \(2\times 2\) matrix, for example <code>matrix([1,2],[3,4])</code>.</p>
<p>
[[input:ansIA]]
[[validation:ansIA]]
[[feedback:prtIA]]
</p>

<p><b>5.</b> Compute \((I-A)^{-1}\).</p>
<p>
[[input:ansInv]]
[[validation:ansInv]]
[[feedback:prtInv]]
</p>

<p><b>6.</b> Use
\[
x_{\mathrm{total}}=(I-A)^{-1}x_0
\]
to estimate the total number of TB cases over all generations, including the initial outbreak.</p>
<p>
[[input:ansTot]]
[[validation:ansTot]]
[[feedback:prtTot]]
</p>

<p><em>You may enter exact fractions such as <code>30/11</code>, or decimals to at least 3 decimal places.</em></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>

<p>The model is
\[
x_{n+1}=Ax_n,\qquad
A={@A@},\qquad
x_0={@x0@}.
\]</p>

<p><b>Next generation.</b></p>
\[
x_1=Ax_0
={@A@}{@x0@}
={@x1@}.
\]

<p><b>Second generation.</b></p>
\[
x_2=Ax_1
={@A@}{@x1@}
={@x2@}.
\]

<p><b>Matrix geometric series.</b></p>
<p>{@proof_display(taProof, proof_steps)@}</p>

<p><b>Compute \(I-A\).</b></p>
\[
I-A={@I2@}-{@A@}={@IA@}.
\]

<p><b>Compute the inverse.</b></p>
\[
(I-A)^{-1}={@IAinv@}.
\]

<p><b>Total cases.</b></p>
\[
x_{\mathrm{total}}
=(I-A)^{-1}x_0
={@IAinv@}{@x0@}
={@xtotal@}.
\]
<p>So the model predicts a total of \({@xtotal[1,1]@}\) Nairobi cases and \({@xtotal[2,1]@}\) Mombasa cases over all generations.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
